Threat vs Vulnerability Analysis 

1. An employee receives an email from “HR
Department” asking to verify their login details
via a link. - THREAT

2.  A company server is running Windows Server
2012, which no longer receives security updates. - VULNERABILITY

3.  A developer accidentally uploads API keys to a
public GitHub repository. - VULNERABILTY

4. A hacker uses a botnet to flood a website with
traffic until it becomes unavailable. - THREAT 

5. The firewall in a branch office is misconfigured to
allow all inbound traffic. - VULNERABILTY

6.An insider copies confidential customer data
onto a personal USB drive - THREAT

7.  The organization’s password policy allows users
to set “12345” as their password. - VULNERABILITY

8.  Cybercriminals send ransomware through email
attachments to multiple employees. - THREAT 

9. A company website doesn’t validate user input in
its contact form, allowing malicious SQL
commands. - VULNERABILITY 

10. Attackers use fake job advertisements on social
media to trick users into sharing personal data. - THREAT
